course: dictionary
lesson: 9345
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Read the words around the word and ask which meaning fits best.
explain: «Spiritual but not religious» describes a person who does not belong to or attend any organised religion. The word spiritual here is about the person's inner feelings and soul, not their body or their things.
explain: «Crossed over» means died; it is a gentle, often spiritual phrase. Words like this are chosen to be kind, so the reader is not frightened by a harsh word.
fact: Spiritual means to do with the human spirit, feelings and soul, rather than the body or things you own.
fact: Spiritual can also mean to do with religion or deep beliefs, as in a spiritual leader.
fact: A spiritual is a religious song first sung by enslaved African Americans, such as «Swing Low, Sweet Chariot».
fact: Spirituals were an important type of song that led to gospel and the blues.
fact: In religious education, spiritual development is about values, wonder and meaning.
exercise: Mia says «Swing Low, Sweet Chariot» is a spiritual. What is a spiritual here? | *A religious song first sung by enslaved African Americans | A type of spinning top | A large bird from the desert | A kind of sweet dessert
exercise: «Spiritual but not religious» describes someone who does what? | Never sings or plays music | Lives on a spaceship | *Does not belong to or attend any organised religion | Attends church every day
exercise: In music lessons, why are spirituals important? | They are songs about the weather | *They are a type of song that led to gospel and the blues | They are the only songs ever written in the desert | They are songs with no tunes at all
exercise: Ben says a spiritual leader is good at football. What does spiritual mean in spiritual leader? | To do with the weather | *To do with religion or deep beliefs | To do with the body and muscles | To do with money and things you own
test: Which phrase is a gentle way of saying someone died? | Crossed out | Crossed arms | Crossed the road | *Crossed over
test: Which meaning of spiritual fits «She felt a deep spiritual peace as the sun set over the hills»? | To do with a sports team | To do with a cheap, sugary drink | *To do with the human spirit and feelings, not the body | To do with a ghost in a haunted house
exam: Which sentence uses spiritual to mean to do with the human spirit and feelings, not the body? | He wore a spiritual hat to school | The runner's legs ached after the race | *Watching the waves, she felt a spiritual calm inside | The spiritual shop sells shoes and hats
